Box:
\boxed{\begin{cases}
\text{If }K>1: \lambda=0\text{ is the unique global minimizer; no finite maximizer (}\sup\psi=1/2\text{ as }|\lambda|\to\infty).\
\text{If }0<K<1: \lambda=0\text{ is the unique global maximizer; no finite minimizer (}\inf\psi=1/2\text{ as }|\lambda|\to\infty).\
\text{If }K=1: \psi(\lambda)=1/2\text{ for all }\lambda.
\end{cases}}

Let's decide final answer assuming K>0:

\boxed{
\begin{array}{ll}
K>1: & \lambda=0 \text{ is the unique global minimizer; } \sup_{\lambda}\psi=1/2 \text{ not attained.}\
0<K<1: & \lambda=0 \text{ is the unique global maximizer; } \inf_{\lambda}\psi=1/2 \text{ not attained.}\
K=1: & \psi(\lambda)=1/2 \text{ for all } \lambda.
\end{array}}
